"\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49538/selection/9928ca17ea5ff34ade2b5209cb69fea6c8c7ff94aac815bde54c043294ff288e" :answer/id #uuid "5c9bde72-c1d5-5074-ae9d-fd1641e26fa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49538/selection/b71516002bf9556e755dfc4216b4d82a0b2c2758b93f9b826bd24f22791ce42d" :answer/id #uuid "43d29deb-5bdd-560c-8aa3-4f859da026e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49538/selection/4cc7e9cdf8fc798c46121d8cc24cb7b6b447dbeec11b5eb40acaf775a842d9c8" :answer/id #uuid "72414d77-03d6-5b39-91e3-43f281283f68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49538/selection/3b28495977b1653d3b265084c301e2471a25911cfc996ab9fb4d1bd2f087ac51" :answer/id #uuid "bb01d264-9c8c-513f-9973-0c007fab95a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49538/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7fdeeb1-9063-51cb-880e-582870afde61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49538/selection/4cc7e9cdf8fc798c46121d8cc24cb7b6b447dbeec11b5eb40acaf775a842d9c8" :answer-field/choices ["q-49538/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-49538/selection/9928ca17ea5ff34ade2b5209cb69fea6c8c7ff94aac815bde54c043294ff288e" "q-49538/selection/b71516002bf9556e755dfc4216b4d82a0b2c2758b93f9b826bd24f22791ce42d" "q-49538/selection/4cc7e9cdf8fc798c46121d8cc24cb7b6b447dbeec11b5eb40acaf775a842d9c8" "q-49538/selection/3b28495977b1653d3b265084c301e2471a25911cfc996ab9fb4d1bd2f087ac51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49538" :question/id #uuid "b78003dc-845c-57d9-8ac3-a4f2236098d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49538" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $4{x}^{2}=(2x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{1+(2x)^{2}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-49538/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2f9806d-3a72-5f0a-a6f4-db8dad8871f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49538"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346458/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer/id #uuid "4e811957-3537-5ea5-9cc8-a914c4846733" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346458/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "99344a88-225a-56e8-a799-6537b9be6eff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346458/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer-field/choices ["q-346458/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346458" :question/id #uuid "ed47f00d-bd2e-5aba-b046-6f14e9853d8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-346458" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{100-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{100-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{100\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/100)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{10}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/100}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/10)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{10})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{10}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{10}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=10\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{100-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/10)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346458/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2f9806d-3a72-5f0a-a6f4-db8dad8871f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346458"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114078/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" :answer/id #uuid "8736ece3-310d-5c9d-bb4b-d50af6dbf9b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114078/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" :answer/id #uuid "b47a60c2-2da3-580d-976e-b576c2f65795" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114078/selection/655610c33f9ee70bd034b89a5aa2c6ed9461fb56dcb4fb9b8027be65bbde5b10" :answer/id #uuid "62b7abb7-da23-591f-97f8-57d989abd28e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114078/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "9f1df431-339e-5d08-b70a-6a4b0efbc5d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114078/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "7e44bb33-fe19-5182-b21a-6f3f76609df7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114078/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a0ea3a4-63e3-5c65-acb6-1b0c3655603f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114078/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-114078/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" "q-114078/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" "q-114078/selection/655610c33f9ee70bd034b89a5aa2c6ed9461fb56dcb4fb9b8027be65bbde5b10" "q-114078/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-114078/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114078" :question/id #uuid "a32b8631-d1be-5b85-884d-c14bcb1ed1c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114078" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/8)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/8}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{8})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{8})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114078/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2f9806d-3a72-5f0a-a6f4-db8dad8871f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114078"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
